   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Routine and separable verbs",
     "texto": [
      "In Dutch, many everyday verbs are separable, much like English «get up»: the prefix separates from the verb and goes to the end of the main clause. «Opstaan» (to get up) is conjugated: «Ik sta om zeven uur op» (the prefix «op» goes at the end). To give the exact time of an action, use the preposition «om»: «om zeven uur» (at seven o'clock). To say where you study: «thuis» (at home)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
